Project Overview:
In terms of my projects, let me give you a business overview of one. Earlier, when customers made purchases
on e-commerce websites, they had to enter their full credit or debit card details, which were stored by the
websites and became vulnerable to unauthorized access. My project introduced tokenization, which hides the
12-digit card number and only displays the last four digits. This eliminates the need to enter the CVV and
greatly enhances security by protecting sensitive information from unauthorized users.
Project Migration:
I'm currently working in the banking domain for my client, JPMorgan Chase. Their requirement was to implement
the Photon framework on Spring Boot applications. Previously, these applications were running on Spring Boot
version 2.7.x, but since Photon only supports version 3.1.x, we had to migrate these applications. This also
involved upgrading from Java 8 to Java 17, as Spring Boot 3.1.x is only compatible with Java 17.

As part of this migration, we worked on multiple applications, performing end-to-end testing, including performance
 and functional testing, and finally moved these applications from development to UAT, and from UAT to production
environments.
